# Kesh Runtime Router

> **Canonical contract:** `rules/kesh-agent-spec.mdc` (v2). Spec wins on conflict.
>
> **Default posture:** Adaptive applicability — minimum sufficient specialists per task class.

## Core Principle

DO NOT match keywords alone. UNDERSTAND intent, assign a **task_class**, then select agents from the class workflow template.

## Triage questions

```
1. WHAT does the user want? (explain / investigate / debug / change / review / design / incident)
2. WHAT is the subject? (code, API, DB, UI, architecture, security)
3. WHAT risk level? (low patch vs schema/security/prod)
4. WHAT depth? (overview / detailed / deep)
5. WHO is asking? (dev / architect / PM) — shapes verbosity, not gates
```

## Flow

```
USER REQUEST
    │
    ▼
EMERGENCY / PRODUCTION_INCIDENT check (explicit)
    │
    ▼
CACHE GATE (kesh-token-cache) — FULL / PARTIAL / MISS / STALE
    │
    ▼
CLASSIFY → task_class
    │
    ▼
SELECT execution_mode (FAST|STANDARD|CRITICAL|INCIDENT_ARCHITECTURE)
      escalate on risk signals — never downgrade for cost
    │
    ▼
SELECT agents from mode + class template
    │
    ▼
BUILD context packages per agent (refs, not full dumps)
    │
    ▼
SELECT standards progressively (scripts/standards/select_standards.py)
    │
    ▼
Knowledge gate (SUFFICIENT → load; else discover → propose MDC)
    │
    ▼
DETERMINISTIC CHECKS first (lint/test/type) when available
    │
    ▼
EXECUTE (parallel only for independent agents actually invoked)
    │
    ▼
CONSOLIDATE → delivery status + report (mode + CACHE + verification)
```

Helpers: `scripts/modes/select_mode.py`, `scripts/context/package.py`, `scripts/standards/select_standards.py`, `scripts/cache/*`.

## Task classes

`EXPLANATION` `INVESTIGATION` `DEBUGGING` `PATCH` `BUG_FIX` `FEATURE` `REFACTOR` `ARCHITECTURE` `DATABASE_CHANGE` `SECURITY_CHANGE` `PRODUCTION_INCIDENT` `CODE_REVIEW`

Full templates: `kesh-agent-spec.mdc`.

